# With spaces, project - away is not an operator name (D-026): DS0104 with a fix, and it parses as project-away.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | project - away x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    PROJECT_AWAY_OP@9..25
      IDENT@9..16 "project"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      MINUS@17..18 "-"
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..23 "away"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      COLUMN_PATTERN@24..25
        IDENT@24..25 "x"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0104]: operator name `project - away` has spaces in it
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | project - away x
  |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an operator name is one word
  |
  = help: write `project-away`, with no spaces

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | project-away x
which parses without errors
